From 8bf48965aa71a9139541c14bb6a1850404ef9d56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navi48-MacOS contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] radv: Darwin native backend, Mesa half of the Navi48 kext
 ABI (S1c)

Replaces the S1a kernel stubs with the marshaller of NATIVE-S1C-ABI.md:
IOServiceOpen(Navi48Bringup, 'N48N') + Hello, BoCreate/BoFree/CPU map,
GemVa, Ctx, Submit (chunks classified in userspace, >64 IBs split, fence on
the last), WaitSeq loops over the 2 s kernel wait, GEM_METADATA/GEM_OP and
ctx pstate in Mesa, memory info and GB_ADDR_CONFIG from the kernel, the
-errno mapping (Timeout -> -ETIME, Aborted -> -ECANCELED).  The syncobj
provider now signals from kernel seqnos (WAIT_FOR_SUBMIT semantics, clone
shares the handle space, DRM-style -1/errno).  RADV_DARWIN_MOCK=1 runs the
contract's selectors in process for host-side end-to-end tests; the ABI
header is the kext builder's, byte for byte.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
